course: dictionary
lesson: 6315
title: Moss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Moss is a small, soft, green plant with no flowers. It grows in thick, low patches on damp ground, rocks, trees and walls.
explain: Moss has no flowers, seeds or proper roots, so it is a very simple plant. It makes tiny spores to make new plants, and it needs damp, shady places to live.
explain: Moss soaks up water like a sponge, which helps stop soil from washing away. But be careful: moss on rocks and steps is very slippery.
fact: Moss is a small, soft, green plant with no flowers, seeds or proper roots.
fact: «Moss-covered» means covered in moss, like an old garden wall.
fact: Moss soaks up water like a sponge, which helps prevent floods and keeps soil from washing away.
fact: Moss often grows on the shady side of trees and rocks, but do not use it to find your way.
fact: Moss on rocks and steps is very slippery, so take care when you walk on it.
exercise: «Lemmings eat grasses, moss and sedges.» In this sentence, what is moss? | A type of rock | A kind of insect | *A small green plant | A large tree
exercise: Why is moss on steps dangerous? | It makes a loud noise | *It is very slippery | It has sharp spikes | It is very hot
exercise: Which fact about moss is true? | It grows deep under the ground like a carrot | *It has no flowers, seeds or proper roots | It has bright flowers in spring | It is a kind of animal
test: Which kind of place does moss need to grow well? | Places with no water at all | The bottom of a hot oven | Very dry, sunny deserts | *Damp, shady places
test: «Tardigrades, or water bears, are tiny eight-legged animals that often live in moss.» Where do tardigrades often live? | *In moss | In the sky | Far out in space | Inside a volcano
exam: How does moss help to stop floods? | *It soaks up water like a sponge | It floats on top of the water | It pumps water out into rivers | It makes the rain stop falling
